Step 1: Ensure master is clean
git status

Output:
nothing to commit, working tree clean

Step 2: Create a new branch
git branch GitWork

Switch to it:
git checkout GitWork

Step 3: Create hello.xml in GitWork
echo "<message>Hello from GitWork</message>" > hello.xml

Check status:
git status

Step 4: Commit changes in GitWork
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in GitWork"
  
Step 5: Switch to master
git checkout master

Step 6: Create the same file with different content
echo "<message>Hello from Master</message>" > hello.xml

Commit it:
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Added hello.xml in master"
  
Step 7: View the log
git log --oneline --graph --decorate --all
  
Step 8: Compare master and branch
git diff master GitWork

Step 9: Merge GitWork into master
git merge GitWork

Expected output:
CONFLICT (add/add): Merge conflict in hello.xml
Automatic merge failed.

Step 10: Observe conflict markers
cat hello.xml

Expected output:
<<<<<<< HEAD
<message>Hello from Master</message>
=======
<message>Hello from GitWork</message>
>>>>>>> GitWork
  
Step 11: Resolve the conflict
echo "<message>Hello from Master and GitWork</message>" > hello.xml

Step 12: Commit the resolved file
git add hello.xml
git commit -m "Resolved merge conflict"
  
Step 13: Add backup files to .gitignore 
echo "*.orig" >> .gitignore
git add .gitignore
git commit -m "Updated gitignore"
  
Step 14: List all branches
git branch

Step 15: Delete merged branch
git branch -d GitWork

Step 16: View final log
git log --oneline --graph --decorate
